/102012","id":2613931421,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bzW2d","user":{"login":"mmertama","id":7837709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4Mzc3MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7837709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama","html_url":"https://github.com/mmertama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T11:13:35Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T11:13:35Z","body":"You have a call stack attached and that should provide plenty of information where it crashes.  My game itself is written in Godot script that shall never do runtime crash (right?), not to mention I have no idea how to isolate the part that helps you.  That game procedurally generates scenes from non-godot-game-data and when applying navigation maps, it dies. It shall be pretty easy to fix if you is to add an exception where C++ crashes and when GDScript catches it and throws its fatal, I would at least get an runtime error that something went wrong, but that it clearly dies is just a bug in Godot's code.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613931421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.g