_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T12:09:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T12:09:24Z","body":"This is not how our bug triage works, it's a waste of resources to just trial and error issues, so please provide a minimal project to follow the process we have\n\nI'm a developer and this is the way we do development, a call stack isn't enough without actual data, it doesn't show *what* triggers an issue, only *where* it is triggered\n\nSo please provide the requested information or this will be closed","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613945342/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613986294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2613986294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2613986294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bzkP2","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T14:35:47Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T14:35:47Z","body":"The next time you have a crash, try to find a pattern and remember your steps that led to the error, create an empty project and try to repeat the same thing, you may have to import some resources if that is the issue. It is not so easy to recognize the problem from a single dump, even when providing MRP it is not always easy, depending on the complexity of the problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613986294/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614016885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2614016885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2614016885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bzrt1","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T16:15:47Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T16:15:47Z","body":"> You dont sound like a developer, you sound like a error manager :-D Please forward this error to some developer has he will be able to see immediately from the attached call stack where it crashes. There is no need for any \"minimal project\" - in the real world there almost never any minimal-project-candies, available but competent developer figures out bugs - and a good call stack is more than enough to pinpoint crashes.\n\nWhat is this attitude? People are trying to offer input which not only makes your own bug report more complete and informative but which would also help the developers pinpoint the exact issue so it can be fixed in a more prompt manner and you go off and insult someone?\n\nThe point of an MRP is exactly to make it easier for developers to understand the issue. As it allows the developer to replicate the issue while trying to debug and fix the problem. So, instead of trying to debate the relevance or efficacy of an MRP like you're trying to do, how about _you_ put in some more effort instead?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614016885/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614032435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2614032435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2614032435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bzvgz","user":{"login":"mmertama","id":7837709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4Mzc3MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7837709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama","html_url":"https://github.com/mmertama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T17:05:53Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T17:06:09Z","body":"I was confused that the call stack was so eagerly ignored as a relevant information as that has been exactly what would be needed. (And therefore I was wondering if errors are screened by someone that won't fully get its value)\n\nApple etc. asks call stack as it well shows the exact line where the error occurs, especially as it is EXC_BAD_ACCESS, that means either null pointer, dangling pointer or out from array. In theory GDScript shall be free that kind of errors, right? (Script languages should not dump) Therefore it should not be too much effort to check what is happening on that particular line, and as minimum throw an exception. \n\nIm not asking you to get solution why my code is not working, I just ask the process not vanishing to the oblivion. My code is fully procedural scene creation and it is 100% that I do something wrong, but I humbly assume that Godot wont crash whatever I do wrong and hence I wrote this report.\n\nYet that is not showstopper to me, I hope will figure out what I do wrong and then the crash shall disappear, but that do not resolve the underlaying issue that it is possible to write script that do bad memory access. If the problem persist, I suppose easier than writing a MRP is to download sources and build a debug version and look it myself, however that is too much of the sidetrack now. ... Apologies, when I get confused I have tendency to get a bit harsh - in general you do great work. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614032435/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614037620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2614037620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2614037620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bzwx0","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T17:23:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T17:23:49Z","body":"> I was confused that the call stack was so eagerly ignored as a relevant information as that has been exactly what would be needed.\n\nIt was not ignored, I looked at it and it wasn't enough to pinpoint the issue\n\n>  I just ask the process not vanishing to the oblivion\n\nIt won't if you provide the information asked for, which is asked for in *every* case like this\n\n> in general you do great work.\n\nThis is entirely the normal procedure, there's no need to respond in this way ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614037620/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614066979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2614066979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2614066979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bz38j","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T19:00:45Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T19:00:45Z","body":"> Script languages should not dump\n\nShould not but they still can. Since there is an underlying interpreter at work which translates the script into actual internal API calls. If something is wrong in how a certain call your code makes is processed then it is still relevant to know what you did to provoke the error.\n\nAssuming, for a moment... your code is fine and you did nothing wrong then, well, Godot itself did something wrong. But to understand what Godot did that caused the crash, it is still good to know what you did that lead up to the crash. Maybe there is some input sanitation lacking somewhere, maybe you just ran into some very odd corner case which wasn't accounted for in Godot's code, etc, etc, etc.\n\n> If the problem persist, I suppose easier than writing a MRP is to download sources and build a debug version and look it myself, however that is too much of the sidetrack now.\n\nThis is an odd conclusion. Look at the crash dump yourself. You will see the exact call that lead to the crash. That should allow you to look at your own project, see what it is you're doing at that point to then simply create a very small sample project which does exactly what you do in your own project at that point.\n\nFar simpler than trying to debug Godot yourself. Since that would involve you getting to understand the Godot codebase and each codebase has its own unique style, its own unique grammar and approach to doing things. It is simpler for you to understand your own project than it is for you to understand Godot's code. Which is not meant to diminish your abilities or anything like that. It is simply a matter of cold, hard fact that you know your own code better than you know Godot's code.\n\nIf I gave you access to my password manager's source code, you would need some time to get to understand what it is I do in the code, why I do it, etc, etc. Same with your code, Godot itself, etc.\n\nSo... I do not see what is so hard for you about simply creating an MRP. You could've created an MRP in the time it has taken you to debate why it is you do not wish to create one.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614066979/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614073218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2614073218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2614073218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bz5eC","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T19:23:48Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T19:23:48Z","body":"I think we should all take a step back and let the author look at the problem and try to make an MRP if they are able to, I think everything that needs to be said has been so, and this would be nice to solve if we are able to get the necessary information ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614073218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614082183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2614082183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2614082183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bz7qH","user":{"login":"mmertama","id":7837709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4Mzc3MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7837709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama","html_url":"https://github.com/mmertama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T19:59:03Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T19:59:03Z","body":"To be honest the issues with  MRP is that I have no idea how to write one: I have a C++ application (that has nothing to do with Godot) that calculates me game information, polygons, textures, navigation polygons etc.. \n\nThen I have 1000+ lines of GDScript that builds up a level from the data. There are some asserts that validates data and state during that initialization, but those are unable to catch any issues.\n\nThen level starts, I move to a certain position (about the same always), and  kaboom. I.e. I have to load data and play the game before I can get it reproduced, there is no easy way to isolate the problem.\n\nI have a vague understanding that navigation data is not ok (yet assert(map.isValid() etc. passes). I was actually looking the C++ NavMap::get_path but unfortunately code lines did not match (even Im quite confident that I was comparing correctly tagged version - I suspect that there are some macros that mess up the line numbers reported) - with some effort that would be doable,  yet I still think custom debug build would be the easiest. However my next plan is to add more navigation state and date validation to see if anything alarming appears. - I will let you know when I know more.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614082183/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629028808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2629028808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102012","id":2629028808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cs8vI","user":{"login":"mmertama","id":7837709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4Mzc3MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7837709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama","html_url":"https://github.com/mmertama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mmertama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T17:03:12Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T17:03:12Z","body":"I suppose I found something - my code had a bug: there were less vertices than indices when navigation polygons were constructed. However that crashed (and took whole game with it) later only when the navigation path was queried.  When I fixed the amount of vertices, the crash disappeared.  Possibly some extra property/parameter feasibility check could be added to help future bug hunting, but on my behalf this issue could be closed. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629028808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629029281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102012#issuecomment-2629029281","issue_url":"https